# Lyceum research note: the pain and the market

Date: 11 October 2026. Written for the organiser's two asks: explain the pain at Asia level or better, and bring real market research and market intelligence.

Labels: [primary] official document opened and quoted; [secondary] reputable press or vendor page; [estimate] commercial market research, method not inspected; [not verified] primary could not be opened.

## 1. The pain

### 1.1 Malaysia

The brief said "32.2% underemployment". That is skill-related underemployment (graduates in jobs below their qualification). Hours-based underemployment was 0.8%. Keep the two apart in a pitch.

