| AI exposure | 620,000 jobs (18% of 3.5 million in 10 sectors) highly impacted within three to five years | TalentCorp Impact Study 2024, via Malay Mail [secondary] |

What the regulator asks of every programme, MQA Code of Practice for Programme Accreditation, 2nd edition [primary, IIUM-hosted copy]:

- 1.1.2: a programme "must be considered only after a needs assessment has indicated that there is a need"; needs assessment includes "the market demand of a programme".
- 1.2.3: "consult the stakeholders in the development of the curriculum."
- 6.1.6: "conduct internal and external consultations, market needs and graduate employability analyses."
- 7.1.3 and 7.1.4: "continual review of the programme to ensure its currency and relevancy"; the review system "must constructively engage stakeholders, including the alumni and employers as well as external experts".
- In practice the cycle is every three to five years (UiTM study) [secondary].

DOSM's Chief Statistician closed the release with "efforts to align the education system with labour market demands". Today a lecturer's evidence for that alignment is advisory-board minutes and tracer surveys, not employer text.

